### Manual smoke test. Works in VS Code (REST Client) and Visual Studio.
### Change @host to http://localhost:8080 when running via docker compose.

@host = http://localhost:5080

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Create an order — expect 201 with status "Pending"
# @name created
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "cust-1001",
  "sku": "KEYBOARD-87",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 2499.50
}

### Read it back — first call hits the database and populates Redis,
### the second is served from the cache.
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{created.response.body.id}}

### A customer's recent orders
GET {{host}}/api/customers/cust-1001/orders?limit=10

### Validation failure — expect 400 with one entry per bad field
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "",
  "sku": "",
  "quantity": 0,
  "unitPrice": -1
}

### Rejected by the worker: quantity above the manual-approval threshold.
### Create this one with Kafka running, then re-read it a moment later —
### status flips from Pending to Rejected.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "cust-1001",
  "sku": "KEYBOARD-87",
  "quantity": 500,
  "unitPrice": 10.00
}

### Unknown order — expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
